{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Moody Blues and The Guess Who feel like natural next choices because I have repeatedly chosen classic rock hits collections and want more familiar older songs.",
    "Lesley Gore connects with my interest in mid-sixties pop, while Rock And Roll Never Forgets fits my interest in classic rock collections."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Blake Shelton's contemporary country and Enya's atmospheric music do not fit the older pop and rock listening I want today, even though both are best-of collections.",
    "I cannot judge whether Greatest Hits or The Very Best of the A&M Years fits my taste without knowing the artist; a compilation title alone does not make me interested."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat greatest-hits collections as interchangeable, when the artist and musical style are what make those collections appealing to me.",
    "My occasional choices outside classic rock seem to have been taken as a broader interest than I feel right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of classic rock and mid-sixties collections matter more to today's listening than any single album outside that pattern.",
    "There is a difference between something I might enjoy and something I would choose now: Air Supply and Pat Benatar interest me, but today's stronger matches come first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in hits collections but sometimes missed the older pop and classic rock sound that makes me choose them today."
}"}
